{"name":"Bulbasaur","hex":"#73a263","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Bulbasaur","blocks":[{"text":"Bulbasaur, known as Fushigidane  in Japan, is a fictional Pokémon species in Nintendo and Game Freak's Pokémon franchise. First introduced in the video games Pokémon Red and Blue, it was created by Atsuko Nishida with the design finalized by Ken Sugimori. Since Bulbasaur's debut, it has appeared in multiple games including Pokémon Go and the Pokémon Trading Card Game, as well as various merchandise and the 1996 anime. In media related to the franchise, Bulbasaur has been voiced by various voice actors, including Megumi Hayashibara in Japanese, and Tara Sands and Michele Knotz in English."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Pok%C3%A9mon_Bulbasaur_art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulbasaur","wikidata":"Q847571"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/ANA_B767-381_JA8578_Pokemon-Jet98.jpg/500px-ANA_B767-381_JA8578_Pokemon-Jet98.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/ANA_B767-381_JA8578_Pokemon-Jet98.jpg/500px-ANA_B767-381_JA8578_Pokemon-Jet98.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bulbasaur has been used heavily in promotion for the series, such as on the side of planes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AANA_B767-381_JA8578_Pokemon-Jet98.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Green Long Legged Fly on Leaf","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Green_Long_Legged_Fly_on_Leaf.jpg/500px-Green_Long_Legged_Fly_on_Leaf.jpg","ratio":1.2064631956912029,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Long_Legged_Fly_on_Leaf.jpg","share":0.23625},{"title":"Pseudatelus sp.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia